$y=f(x)+c$ with $c>0$ shifts the graph **up** $c$ units and $y=f(x)-c$ shifts it **down**, mapping $(x,y)\to(x,y\pm c)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-3.6,0) -- (3.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.2) -- (0,4.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,gray,dashed,<->,domain=-2.7:2.7,smooth,samples=61,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2-0.5*\x*\x});
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-2.95:2.95,smooth,samples=61,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{3.2-0.5*\x*\x});
\draw[->] (-0.6,1.82) -- (-0.6,3.02) node[midway,left] {$c$};
\node[blue,right] at (-3.5,3.75) {$y=f(x)+c$};
\node[gray,right] at (-3.5,2.85) {$y=f(x)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$y=f(x-b)$ with $b>0$ shifts the graph **right** $b$ units and $y=f(x+b)$ shifts it **left**, mapping $(x,y)\to(x\pm b,y)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-3.6,0) -- (5.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.2) -- (0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,gray,dashed,<->,domain=-2.7:2.7,smooth,samples=61,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2-0.5*\x*\x});
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.3:4.1,smooth,samples=61,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2-0.5*(\x-1.4)*(\x-1.4)});
\draw[dotted] (0,2) -- (0,2.6);
\draw[dotted] (1.4,2) -- (1.4,2.6);
\draw[->] (0,2.45) -- (1.4,2.45) node[midway,above] {$b$};
\node[gray,right] at (-3.5,2.7) {$y=f(x)$};
\node[blue,right] at (2.9,2.7) {$y=f(x-b)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

