foundation.solution_text:
$y=f(x)-2$ shifts every point **down** $2$: $(x,y)\to(x,y-2)$.
$(-1,1)\to(-1,-1)$ and $(1,-1)\to(1,-3)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-2.7,0)--(2.7,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.9)--(0,2.9) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,gray,dashed,<->,domain=-2.3:2.3,smooth,samples=61,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.5*\x*\x*\x-1.5*\x});
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-2.0:2.3,smooth,samples=61,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.5*\x*\x*\x-1.5*\x-2});
\node[gray,right] at (1.55,1.2) {$y=f(x)$};
\node[blue,right] at (1.6,-2.6) {$y=f(x)-2$};
\fill[gray] (-1,1) circle (1.5pt);
\fill[gray] (1,-1) circle (1.5pt);
\fill (-1,-1) circle (2pt) node[left] {$(-1,-1)$};
\fill (1,-3) circle (2pt) node[right] {$(1,-3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

